## Rotating Card – CSS Only

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card which flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Container – gives perspective so the 3D effect looks good */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* depth of the 3D space */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – 3D transform origin set to center */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s;    /* smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* 4️⃣  Front & Back faces – positioned back‑to‑back */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front face – normal orientation */
.card-front {
  background: #4a90e2;
}

/* Back face – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.card-back {
  background: #e94e77;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <p>Front</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <p>Back</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives depth to the 3D transform. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| **3** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **4** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the backside of each face when it’s not facing the viewer. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back face | Positions the back face opposite the front so it becomes visible after the flip. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a vertical flip instead, change `rotateY` to `rotateX`.
